SUMMARY:Woody De Othello: coming forth by day
DESCRIPTION:This solo exhibition by the Oakland-based artist featuring a new series of works that explore the primordial relationship between body\, earth and spirit. Othello honors an important Northern California lineage of ceramic artists and expands that tradition by drawing on knowledge and philosophies from around the world through a decolonial lens. Through material experimentation and sculptural gesture\, the exhibition considers how objects carry history\, absorb meaning and serve as vessels for both spiritual and emotional experience. \n“Woody De Othello: coming forth by day” is organized by Pérez Art Museum Miami. The Manetti Shrem Museum presentation is organized by Susie Kantor\, associate curator and exhibition department head. \nOpen 10am – 5pm\, Wednesday through Saturday. Click here for holiday hours.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/woody-de-othello-coming-forth-by-day/
LOCATION:Jan Shrem and Maria Manetti Shrem Museum of Art at UC Davis\, 254 Old Davis Road\, Davis\, California\, 95616
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/WDO-install-Oriol-Tarridas.-lo-rez.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Jan Shrem and Maria Manetti Shrem Museum of Art at UC Davis%E2%80%8E":MAILTO:manettishrem@ucdavis.edu
END:VEVENT
